// Typed lists and queues ('a queue of string'), the type Any, and names for the effects of a Then:
//   '… is executed with inputs job' names what the user inputs, of the type the action declares for that input;
//   '… is dequeued as job' names the dequeued element, of the element type of its queue.
// Only Any converts to another type: a variable of type Any where a type is needed is a warning, and Z3 takes it as
// a value of that type. Any other mismatch is an error (see type-errors.easy).
// Expected: 'Schedule job' and 'Submit job' have no problem;
//           'Untyped item': a warning, 'item' can be any value, but 'speed' is an int (Z3: fine, if item is an int);
//           'Tune speed': a warning, 'level' can be any value, but 'speed' is an int (Z3: fine, if level is an int).

Entity Printer {
    Actions: start
    Data properties: speed: int, note: Any, inbox: a queue, waiting jobs: a queue of string, scheduled jobs: a queue of string
}

Role Operator.

Action start { Initiators: Operator }
Action submit { Initiators: Operator, Input: job: string }
Action tune { Initiators: Operator, Input: level: Any }

// the first waiting job goes to the end of the scheduled jobs: both hold strings
Scenario: Schedule job
Given start is available
When start is executed
Then the Printer's waiting jobs is dequeued as job
    AND the Printer's scheduled jobs is enqueued with job.

// the inbox holds Any, so the item may or may not be an int
Scenario: Untyped item
Given start is available
When start is executed
Then the Printer's inbox is dequeued as item
    AND the Printer's speed is set to item
    AND the Printer's note is set to item.

// what the user inputs is a string, as the waiting jobs are
Scenario: Submit job
Given submit is available
When submit is executed with inputs job
Then the Printer's waiting jobs is enqueued with job.

// tune takes any value, so the level may or may not be an int
Scenario: Tune speed
Given tune is available
When tune is executed with inputs level
Then the Printer's speed is set to level.
